-- title:
--   Chart functions vanishing mod mathfrak m_A lie in a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $q\ell$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$, and let $K \subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ be the intermediate field over $L$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars $\mathbb Q \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $j \in K$ be the nonzero element whose Laurent series is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Consider the two-chart integral model $X$ over $A$ attached to $(K,j)$, obtained by glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ to that of $A[j^{-1}]$ along the middle chart. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ at which the germ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y \in \operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra $C$ map to $z$. Assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel exactly the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in the set of $\Omega$-invariants $j_0$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then every $a \in C$ all of whose Laurent coefficients, in every integer degree, lie in $\operatorname{image}(\mathfrak m_A \to L)$ belongs to the prime ideal $y$.
--
--   This is the local vanishing statement at a supersingular point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model: a function on the finite ($j$-integral) chart whose $q$-expansion has all coefficients in the maximal ideal of the base reduces to zero at that point, hence lies in the corresponding prime. It is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond variant of the auxiliary-level argument, set up so that no lower bound on $q$ is needed, and it feeds the comparison of the Drinfeld chart with the coefficient condition used further on in the construction of the integral model.
